---@class resend.resend.CreateInboxDraftRequest
---@field inbox_id string The Inbox ID or the inbox email address, such as `support@acme.com`. A value that contains `@` must be a valid email address, and any other value must be a UUID, or the request returns a 422. The address match is case-insensitive and never falls back to the inbox `name`. An address that matches no inbox returns a 404.
---@field idempotencyKey? string A unique key for the request, so the draft is created only once. A retry with the same key within 24 hours returns the first successful (2xx) response, with the `idempotent-replayed: true` header. A failed request is not stored, so it can be retried with the same key. Reusing the key with a different body, or while the first request is still running, returns a 409. An empty key, or one longer than 256 characters, returns a 400 `invalid_idempotency_key`. [Learn more](https://resend.com/docs/dashboard/emails/idempotency-keys)
---@field to? resend.resend.CreateInboxDraftRequestTo|distilled.Null The recipients. For multiple addresses, send an array of strings. Each value can include a friendly name, for example `Ada Lovelace <ada@example.org>`. Each address is `email@example.com` or `Name <email@example.com>`. An address that is not valid returns a 422.
---@field cc? resend.resend.CreateInboxDraftRequestCc|distilled.Null The CC recipients. For multiple addresses, send an array of strings. Each address is `email@example.com` or `Name <email@example.com>`. An address that is not valid returns a 422.
---@field bcc? resend.resend.CreateInboxDraftRequestBcc|distilled.Null The BCC recipients. For multiple addresses, send an array of strings. Each address is `email@example.com` or `Name <email@example.com>`. An address that is not valid returns a 422.
---@field subject? string|distilled.Null The subject. Max 2000 characters. A string that is only whitespace, or that contains a line break, is rejected.
---@field html? string|distilled.Null The HTML body.
---@field text? string|distilled.Null The plain text body.
---@field attachments? resend.resend.CreateInboxDraftRequestAttachmentsList|distilled.Null Files to store on the draft. Each one needs a `filename` and either `content` or a `path` URL. A `path` file is downloaded when the request is made and stored on the draft. When both are sent, `path` is ignored. A `content_id` returns a 422. The files on a draft, downloaded ones included, can total at most 25 MB. A `path` that does not start with `http` or `https`, or that cannot be downloaded, returns a 422, and so does a request whose downloads take more than 20 seconds together. An empty file or a blocked file type returns a 422.
---@field thread_id? string The Thread ID to reply in. Must be sent with `reply_to_email_id`.
