---@class resend.resend.ForwardInboxThreadEmailRequest
---@field inbox_id string The Inbox ID or the inbox email address, such as `support@acme.com`. A value that contains `@` must be a valid email address, and any other value must be a UUID, or the request returns a 422. The address match is case-insensitive and never falls back to the inbox `name`. An address that matches no inbox returns a 404.
---@field thread_id string The Thread ID.
---@field email_id string The Email ID of the message to forward, as returned in `data[].id` by the list thread emails endpoint.
---@field idempotencyKey? string A unique key for the request, so the forward is sent only once. A retry with the same key within 24 hours returns the first successful (2xx) response, with the `idempotent-replayed: true` header. A failed request is not stored, so it can be retried with the same key. Reusing the key with a different body, or while the first request is still running, returns a 409. An empty key, or one longer than 256 characters, returns a 400 `invalid_idempotency_key`. [Learn more](https://resend.com/docs/dashboard/emails/idempotency-keys)
---@field to resend.resend.ForwardInboxThreadEmailRequestTo Recipient email address. For multiple addresses, send as an array of strings. Must name at least one address. `to`, `cc` and `bcc` combined cannot exceed 50 recipients. Each address is `email@example.com` or `Name <email@example.com>`. An address that is not valid returns a 422.
---@field cc? resend.resend.ForwardInboxThreadEmailRequestCc|distilled.Null CC recipient email address. For multiple addresses, send as an array of strings. Counts toward the 50-recipient limit. Each address is `email@example.com` or `Name <email@example.com>`. An address that is not valid returns a 422.
---@field bcc? resend.resend.ForwardInboxThreadEmailRequestBcc|distilled.Null BCC recipient email address. For multiple addresses, send as an array of strings. Counts toward the 50-recipient limit. Each address is `email@example.com` or `Name <email@example.com>`. An address that is not valid returns a 422.
---@field html? string An HTML note sent above the quoted original.
---@field text? string A plain-text note sent above the quoted original.
---@field subject? string The subject of the forward. Cannot be only whitespace or contain a line break. When omitted, the thread subject is used, prefixed with `Fwd:` if it does not already start with it.
---@field attachments? resend.resend.ForwardInboxThreadEmailRequestAttachmentsList|distilled.Null Files to attach, as on `POST /emails`. Each one needs `content` or `path`. They share one limit with the attachments of the original message, which the forward also sends. Together they can have at most 25 MB of `content`. A `path` file does not count toward the 25 MB, because it is fetched when the email is sent. An empty file, a blocked file type, a `path` that does not start with `http` or that starts with `http://localhost:`, or a `content_type` that is not a valid MIME type returns a 422. Other `path` problems fail the email when it is sent, not the request.
---@field headers? resend.resend.ForwardInboxThreadEmailRequestHeadersMap|distilled.Null Custom headers to add to the email. The `In-Reply-To`, `References` and `Reply-To` headers are set by Resend and cannot be set here. Sending one of them, in any letter case, returns a 422. Header names cannot be empty, and names and values cannot contain line breaks or null characters, or the request returns a 422. `null` means no custom headers.

