---@class resend.resend.SearchInboxThreadsRequest
---@field inbox_id string The Inbox ID or the inbox email address, such as `support@acme.com`. A value that contains `@` must be a valid email address, and any other value must be a UUID, or the request returns a 422. The address match is case-insensitive and never falls back to the inbox `name`. An address that matches no inbox returns a 404.
---@field query? string Free text to search for in the subject, body, sender, recipients, and attachment names. Every word must match. Wrap words in double quotes to match an exact phrase. Start a word or quoted phrase with `-` to exclude it. Max 256 characters and 32 words.
---@field from? resend.resend.SearchInboxThreadsRequestFromList Comma-separated senders. Each value matches part of the sender's address or name, without case. Returns threads that match any of them. Up to 20 values. Repeating the parameter returns a 422 validation_error.
---@field to? resend.resend.SearchInboxThreadsRequestToList Comma-separated recipients, matched the same way as `from`. Up to 20 values. Repeating the parameter returns a 422 validation_error.
---@field cc? resend.resend.SearchInboxThreadsRequestCcList Comma-separated CC recipients, matched the same way as `from`. Up to 20 values. Repeating the parameter returns a 422 validation_error.
---@field bcc? resend.resend.SearchInboxThreadsRequestBccList Comma-separated BCC recipients, matched the same way as `from`. Up to 20 values. Repeating the parameter returns a 422 validation_error.
---@field has_attachment? boolean `true` matches emails with an attachment. `false` matches emails without one. Only the literal values `true` and `false` are accepted.
---@field start_date? string Matches emails sent on or after this date. Accepts a date like `2026-09-01` or an ISO 8601 timestamp, in UTC unless the timestamp has an offset. An empty value returns a 422.
---@field end_date? string Matches emails sent on or before this date. Same formats as `start_date`. A date covers that whole day, so `start_date=2026-09-01&end_date=2026-09-30` covers all of September. A timestamp is used as given. An `end_date` before `start_date` returns a 422 validation_error. An empty value returns a 422.
---@field folders? resend.resend.SearchInboxThreadsRequestFoldersList Comma-separated folders to search, for example `inbox,sent`. Repeating the parameter returns a 422 validation_error. A thread is returned when any of its emails is in one of the folders. Defaults to `inbox`, or to `inbox,archive,sent` when `labels` is set. `spam` and `trash` are only included when you name them.
---@field labels? resend.resend.SearchInboxThreadsRequestLabelsList Comma-separated label IDs. Returns threads with any of these labels. Up to 50 IDs. An ID that does not exist in the inbox returns a 404. Repeating the parameter returns a 422 validation_error.
---@field read? boolean `true` returns threads where every email is read. `false` returns threads with at least one unread email. Only the literal values `true` and `false` are accepted.
---@field limit? number Number of items to return.
---@field after? string Return items after this cursor.
---@field before? string Return items before this cursor.

